@startsalt
' Screen: Rubric Editor
' User Stories:
'   - As a test engineer, I can define a rubric name, slug, and description
'   - As a test engineer, I can choose a judge prompt and model for automated scoring
'   - As a test engineer, I can select between continuous or ladder scale types
'   - As a test engineer, I can define ordered ladder labels with numeric values
'   - As a test engineer, I can add weighted criteria to a rubric
'   - As a test engineer, I can preview scoring against a sample before publishing

{
  {
    <b>codefre.sh</b> | Scripts | Prompts | Rubrics | Personas | Runs | Settings
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Edit Rubric</b> — RAG Faithfulness | [< Back to Rubrics] | " " | [Save Draft] | [Publish v4]
  }
  ==
  {
    {
      <b>Identity</b>
      --
      Name        | "RAG Faithfulness                              "
      Slug        | "rag-faithfulness                              " | <i>(auto-generated, editable)</i>
      Description | "Measures whether the model response is grounded in the provided context. Penalizes hallucination and unsupported claims." | " "
      " "         | " "
      <b>Judge Configuration</b>
      --
      Judge Prompt | ^rag-faithfulness-judge-v2 (published)^   | [Change...]
      Judge Model  | ^gpt-4o-mini^                             | [Change...]
      Temperature  | "0.0  "
      " "          | " "
      <b>Scale Type</b>
      --
      (X) Ladder (discrete labels)   () Continuous (numeric range)
      " "
      <b>Ladder Labels</b> <i>(ordered high → low, value in parentheses)</i>
      --
      [↑] [↓] | Excellent  | = | 5 | [Remove]
      [↑] [↓] | Good       | = | 4 | [Remove]
      [↑] [↓] | Fair       | = | 3 | [Remove]
      [↑] [↓] | Poor       | = | 2 | [Remove]
      [↑] [↓] | Fail       | = | 1 | [Remove]
      [+ Add Label]
      " "
      <b>Criteria</b> <i>(weights must sum to 100%)</i>
      --
      <b>Label</b>             | <b>Description</b>                                              | <b>Weight</b>
      Groundedness      | "Response claims are traceable to provided context."   | "40 " | %
      Completeness      | "All key facts from context are represented."          | "35 " | % | [Remove]
      Conciseness       | "No redundant or off-topic content."                   | "25 " | % | [Remove]
      [+ Add Criterion]
      " "
      <i>Total weight: 100% ✓</i>
    }
    |
    {
      <b>Preview Scoring</b>
      --
      <b>Sample Input (user message)</b>
      {+
        "What is the capital of France?"
      }
      " "
      <b>Sample Context</b>
      {+
        "France is a country in Western Europe. Its capital city is Paris, which is also its largest city."
      }
      " "
      <b>Model Response</b>
      {+
        "The capital of France is Paris."
      }
      " "
      [Score Now]
      " "
      <b>Score Result</b>
      --
      {+
        Overall:      Excellent (5)
        Groundedness: Excellent — response directly cites context
        Completeness: Good — covers main fact
        Conciseness:  Excellent — minimal and precise
        " "
        Raw judge output:
        <i>"The response correctly identifies Paris as the capital,</i>
        <i>fully supported by the provided context. Score: 5."</i>
      }
    }
  }
}

@endsalt
